+A \memph{thin annulus} is a set of the form $\gc(a,\gamma)\setminus\go(a,\gamma)=\{x\in\VF:\vv(x-a)=\gamma\}$, where $a\in\VF$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma$. Equivalently, it is a closed disc with one maximal open subdisc removed.
+
 \begin{lem}[{\cite[Lemma~3.8]{Yin:int:acvf}}]\label{hae:component:11}
 Let $A \sub \VF$ be an atomic open disc or an atomic closed disc or an atomic thin annulus. Let $f : A \fun \VF$ be a definable function. Then $f(A)$ is also atomic of one of these three forms.
 \end{lem}
